/*  Records — `a record with (…)`, `a series of records like (…)`, `the <field> of`, `the first of`,
    and setting a field.

    ★ A record is a VALUE, as an object is: `Define truck as car` makes a second record, so setting
      a field of one leaves the other alone. In C it is a struct, copied as structs are.

    ★ Its kind is written `record(<part>;<part>;…)`: a positional field's kind, then each named one
      as `<name>=<kind>`, the named ones SORTED by name — the order the language keeps them in and
      prints them in, so two records of the same fields are one kind whatever order they were
      written in. A part may hold another record; parts are split only outside brackets.

    ★ A record's struct is written with the unions, after the objects it may hold. An object
      cannot hold a record yet, for the same reason it cannot hold a union.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to is-record, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "record(".
    Done.

    /// A record's parts, in order — split at each `;` that is not inside another record's brackets.
    Bind series of text to record-parts, given (the text kind):
        Define inner as the characters from 8 to (the length of kind - 1) of kind.
        Define parts as a series of text.
        If inner is "", return parts.
        Define depth as 0.
        Define begun as 1.
        Define place as 0.
        Define total as the length of inner.
        While place is less than total, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define letter as the characters from place to place of inner.
            If letter is "(", increment depth by 1.
            If letter is ")", decrement depth by 1.
            If letter is ";" and depth is 0:
                Insert (the characters from begun to (place - 1) of inner) into parts.
                The begun becomes place + 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert (the characters from begun to total of inner) into parts.
        Return parts.
    Done.

    /// A part's name, or "" for a positional one. A name holds no space and no bracket.
    Bind text to part-name, given (the text part):
        Define equals as the position of "=" in part but void is 0.
        If equals is 0, return "".
        Define named as the characters from 1 to (equals - 1) of part.
        If named contains " " or named contains "(", return "".
        Return named.
    Done.

    /// A part's kind.
    Bind text to part-kind, given (the text part):
        Define named as cast part-name on (part).
        If named is "", return part.
        Return the characters from (the length of named + 2) to the end of part.
    Done.

    /// The kind of a named field, or "" when the record has none of that name.
    Bind text to record-field-kind, given (the text kind, the text field-name):
        For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
            If cast part-name on (part) is field-name, return cast part-kind on (part).
        Done.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// How many positional fields a record has — they come first.
    Bind number to positional-count, given (the text kind):
        Define counted as 0.
        For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
            If cast part-name on (part) is "", increment counted by 1.
        Done.
        Return counted.
    Done.

    /// A record kind from its positional kinds and its named ones, the named sorted by name.
    Bind text to record-kind-of, given (the series of text positional, the map from text to text named):
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each pair in named, repeat:
            Insert the key of pair into names.
        Done.
        Define joined-parts as "".
        For each part in positional, repeat:
            If joined-parts is "", the joined-parts becomes part.
            Otherwise, the joined-parts becomes "{joined-parts};{part}".
        Done.
        For each field-name in names sorted, repeat:
            Define part as "{field-name}={the entry for field-name in named but void is ""}".
            If joined-parts is "", the joined-parts becomes part.
            Otherwise, the joined-parts becomes "{joined-parts};{part}".
        Done.
        Return "record({joined-parts})".
    Done.

    Bind text to record-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define named as "crec".
        For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
            Define field-name as cast part-name on (part).
            If field-name is "", the named becomes "{named}_p{cast c-tag on (part)}".
            Otherwise, the named becomes "{named}_n{cast c-ident on (field-name)}_{cast c-tag on (cast part-kind on (part))}".
        Done.
        Return named.
    Done.

    /// The C member a part is held in: `p<n>` for the nth positional one, the name's for a named one.
    Bind text to record-member, given (the text part, the number place):
        Define field-name as cast part-name on (part).
        If field-name is "", return "p{place}".
        Return cast c-name on (field-name).
    Done.

    /// Notes a record type the program uses, so its struct, and its series', are written.
    Bind void to register-record unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Whether a record can hold a kind — anything this compiler holds by value or by address.
    Bind fact to is-field-kind, given (the text kind):
        Return cast is-element-kind on (kind) or cast element-of on (kind) is not "" or cast is-map on (kind)
            or cast is-voidable on (kind).
    Done.

    /// A record's struct, and how it is written and compared.
    Bind text to c-record-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast record-c-name on (kind).
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "typedef struct \{" into out.
        If the number of cast record-parts on (kind) is 0, insert " char cf_nothing;" into out.
        Define writes as a chase.
        Define tests as "1".
        Define place as 0.
        For each part in cast record-parts on (kind), repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define field-name as cast part-name on (part).
            Define held as cast part-kind on (part).
            Define member as cast record-member on (part, place).
            Insert " {cast c-type on (held)} {member};" into out.
            If place is greater than 1, insert " fputs(\", \", stdout);" into writes.
            If field-name is not "", insert " fputs(\"{field-name}: \", stdout);" into writes.
            Insert " {cast write-call on (held, "r.{member}")};" into writes.
            The tests becomes "{tests} && {cast c-equal on (held, "a.{member}", "b.{member}")}".
        Done.
        Insert " \} {type-c};\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {type-c}_write({type-c} r) \{ fputs(\"record(\", stdout);{writes converted to text} fputs(\")\", stdout); \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static int {type-c}_eq({type-c} a, {type-c} b) \{ return {tests}; \}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind of a written record type.
    Bind text or failure to record-kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        Define positional as a series of text.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define held as cast one's kind-of-type on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-field-kind on (held) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record holding a {held}")).
            Insert held into positional.
        Done.
        Define named as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (written, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define held as cast one's kind-of-type on (item 2 of pair's children) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-field-kind on (held) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record holding a {held}")).
            In named, the entry for cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children) becomes held.
        Done.
        Define kind as cast record-kind-of on (positional, named).
        Cast one's register-record on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// The kind of `a record with (…)`.
    Bind text or failure to record-literal-kind unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define positional as a series of text.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define held as cast one's kind-of on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-field-kind on (held) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record holding a {held}")).
            Insert held into positional.
        Done.
        Define named as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define held as cast one's kind-of on (item 2 of pair's children) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-field-kind on (held) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record holding a {held}")).
            In named, the entry for cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children) becomes held.
        Done.
        Define kind as cast record-kind-of on (positional, named).
        Cast one's register-record on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// `a record with (…)` as C — each field into its member.
    Bind text or failure to c-record-literal unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as cast one's record-literal-kind on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define assigned as "".
        Define place as 0.
        For each inner in (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define value as cast one's c-of on (inner) or pass the failure off.
            If assigned is not "", the assigned becomes "{assigned}, ".
            The assigned becomes "{assigned}.p{place} = {value}".
        Done.
        For each pair in (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Define value as cast one's c-of on (item 2 of pair's children) or pass the failure off.
            If assigned is not "", the assigned becomes "{assigned}, ".
            The assigned becomes "{assigned}.{cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (item 1 of pair's children))} = {value}".
        Done.
        If assigned is "", return "(({cast record-c-name on (kind)})\{ 0 \})".
        Return "(({cast record-c-name on (kind)})\{ {assigned} \})".
    Done.

    /// The positional part a place names — the last one when there is no place.
    Bind text or failure to positional-part unto emitter, given (the text kind, the node index):
        Define count as cast positional-count on (kind).
        Define place as count.
        If cast is-nothing on (index) is false:
            If index's kind is not "NumberLiteral", return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record's field reached by a computed place")).
            The place becomes (cast field-of on (index, 1))'s word converted to number but void is 0.
        Done.
        If place < 1 or place > count, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a record's field {place} of {count}")).
        Return "{place}".
    Done.

    /// The kind of `the first of <record>`, and its C.
    Bind text or failure to record-item-kind unto emitter, given (the text kind, the node index):
        Define place as (cast one's positional-part on (kind, index) or pass the failure off) converted to number but void is 1.
        Return item place of cast record-parts on (kind).
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to c-record-item unto emitter, given (the text record-c, the text kind, the node index):
        Define place as cast one's positional-part on (kind, index) or pass the failure off.
        Return "({record-c}).p{place}".
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `The <field> of <record> becomes <value>.`
    Bind void or failure to emit-record-set unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define field-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define target-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If cast object-of on (target-kind) is not "":
            Define as-field-set as cast made on ("PossessiveSetStatement", a series with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 1), cast field-of on (statement, 3))).
            Cast one's emit-field-set on (as-field-set) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-record on (target-kind) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("setting the {field-name} of a {target-kind}")).
        If cast is-place on (target) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("setting a field of something that is not a name")).
        Define held as cast record-field-kind on (target-kind, field-name).
        If held is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("the {field-name} of a {target-kind}")).
        Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), held) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's line on ("({target-c}).{cast c-name on (field-name)} = {value};").
    Done.
Done.
